{# The attributes that make a page's pill of links -- Home's feeds, the
   hashtag orders, the documents -- switch the page in place: the links
   are boosted, and what comes back is morphed into the content area
   (main.ds-content) rather than swapped for the whole body, so the
   toolbar is untouched and the content keeps what it can. The pill
   itself is skipped by the morph (hx-morph-skip): it is already showing
   the new choice, its thumb sliding to it (segmented.jinja), and the
   response's copy of it would stop the slide where it stands. Fetched
   ahead on hover or touch (hx-preload); the content area dims while a
   fetch that was not ahead is on its way (hx-indicator, ds.css). The
   address is pushed as for any boosted link, and going back is htmx's,
   from its history cache where it has the page. And nothing is scrolled
   (show:none): htmx gives every boosted swap `show:top`, which calls
   scrollIntoView on the content area and moves the page under the sticky
   header by however far it is from the top -- the pill slipping up behind
   the toolbar at every switch.

   htmx 4 is too new for the oldest browsers the site serves (Firefox 56),
   and there these are ordinary links. #}
{% macro in_place() -%}
hx-boost:inherited="true" hx-target:inherited="main.ds-content" hx-select:inherited="main.ds-content" hx-swap:inherited="outerMorph show:none" hx-indicator:inherited="main.ds-content" hx-preload:inherited="mouseover, touchstart" hx-morph-skip
{%- endmacro %}
